---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import AiSystemRiskChecklistTool from '../../components/tools/AiSystemRiskChecklistTool';
---

<ToolLayout
	title="AI System Risk Checklist - Defensive self-assessment | TommyTools"
	description="Free AI system risk checklist: intended use, ownership, data, oversight, access, logging, evaluation, incidents, third parties, and limitations. Transparent scoring and downloadable report. Informal self-assessment - not an audit or certification."
	heading="AI system risk checklist"
	purpose="Work through a structured defensive self-check for an AI system you own or operate. Mark Yes / No / N/A, see gaps and follow-ups, and download a summary report. Informal self-assessment only - not an audit or certification."
	category="AI governance"
	categoryHref="/?tools=ai-governance"
>
	<div slot="tool">
		<AiSystemRiskChecklistTool client:load />
	</div>

	<div slot="instructions">
		<ol>
			<li>Read each section’s <strong>purpose</strong>, then answer the items with Yes, No, or N/A.</li>
			<li>Review completion %, gaps (No answers), and suggested follow-ups.</li>
			<li>Optional: <strong>Save draft locally</strong> in this browser’s localStorage.</li>
			<li>Use <strong>Download report</strong> for a text summary you keep on your device.</li>
		</ol>
	</div>

	<div slot="example">
		<p>
			Example: you answer most items Yes, mark “Is there a named product/system owner?” as{' '}
			<strong>No</strong>. The summary shows a gap for system ownership and suggests assigning a
			primary owner. The downloadable report lists that gap under “GAPS” with the follow-up action -
			it does <em>not</em> claim the system is compliant or certified.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div slot="formula">
		<p>
			<strong>Transparent scoring (not a risk rating):</strong>
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<code>Completion % = answered items / total items</code> (Yes, No, and N/A count as answered)
			</li>
			<li>
				<code>Addressed % = Yes / (Yes + No)</code> among answered items; N/A excluded; null if no
				Yes/No yet
			</li>
			<li>Gaps = items answered <strong>No</strong>; follow-ups come from those items’ guidance</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			A high completion % only means you filled in the form. It does not prove safety or compliance.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div slot="limitations">
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Not an audit, certification, or security guarantee.</strong> Informal self-assessment
				only.
			</li>
			<li>Defensive review prompts - no exploit steps, bypass guidance, or attack tooling.</li>
			<li>No LLM calls; answers are scored with fixed rules in your browser.</li>
			<li>
				Persistence: optional localStorage draft on this device, or download-only report. Nothing is
				uploaded by this tool.
			</li>
			<li>
				Framework-mapped checklists (e.g. NIST AI RMF, OWASP LLM) are separate tools and are not
				claimed here.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>


	<div slot="related">
		<ul class="related-list">
			<li>
				<a href="/tools/nist-ai-rmf-checklist">NIST AI RMF checklist</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="/tools/owasp-llm-top10-checklist">OWASP LLM Top 10 checklist</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>

</ToolLayout>
